## 10. Not verified / remaining risks (judge calls)

- In-game look: nothing here was seen in Minecraft. The evidence is the offline panorama
  (1024x768, 0.35 deg/px) and the 2048x1536 probe; star widths are floored at
  footprint*0.55 = 0.0002 cells*128, so on a 1080p screen the field is ~10x better
  sampled than the panorama and may read differently (denser, sharper).
- The end-fog/void path (end_fog) and the body/ring geometry were left alone, so the
  "universe" gain is all in the sky: star field, ISM band, disc hue and ring texture.
- Star density: measured 2.28 stars/deg^2 total and 0.62/deg^2 in the bright layer
  (local-maxima count at 2048x1536; the analytic cell count is 3.16/deg^2, the gap is
  coincident stars merging into one peak). docs/2026-09-11-end-final-design.md section 3
  asks for 6-10 stars/deg^2 above threshold, which sits in tension with its own
  "large empty areas / sparse" requirement (section 1-2); the sparse reading was kept.
- The photon ring FWHM is 0.39 deg at the probe footprint and ~0.10 deg in game, not the
  1.5%-of-shadow-diameter (0.21 deg) the design doc asks for at its own 12-13 deg shadow
  scale; a 0.21 deg line is sub-pixel at game resolution and would alias. Documented
  deviation, not a silent downgrade.
- Local maxima under-count stars whose Gaussian peaks land on the same pixel; the probe
  density is therefore a lower bound, not an exact count.

